{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSAmu1aGA3HfZJnbWm5D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have the picture now. Before editing, here is what the code and logs show:\n\n- **Connect fails for everyone:** the button is a plain `<a href>`, so the browser navigates without the `Authorization` header, and `auth_init` returns 401 (ticket #214, log section 1).\n- **Authorize step returns 400:** the authorize URL has no `response_type=code`, which OAuth2 requires. The ticket blames the calendar scopes added 2026-10-02, and I can't check that from here.\n- **Rivera's \"expired after an hour\":** the response had no `expires_in` and no `refresh_token`, so the code guessed `DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600`, and the refresher then marked the connection expired.\n- **Stale status on 401:** if Intervals rejects a token on a wellness call, the connection still reports \"connected\".\n- **Config:** `config.py` says the real client pair comes from the deploy env, but nothing reads the env.\n\nI'll make the fixes in `server.py`, `config.py`, and `static/app.js`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5499,"cache_read_input_tokens":30157,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5499},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28a76e9f-8d1a-4338-b383-2fe5082b1be8","uuid":"71312740-a0fa-4d1e-b899-e1e43ea71f9b","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:13:13.391Z","request_id":"req_011CgSAmtjhpybHfWjex6pSH"}
